<mujoco model="straight_corridor">
    <!--
    Minimal two-wall corridor, built specifically to headlessly validate/demo
    examples/track_centering.py. This is scenery ONLY — it does not name the
    car. The demo script attaches neoracer.xml at runtime (see ramp_course.xml
    for the same pattern), so this scene stays independent of the car model.

    Layout (top-down, +X = forward, +Y = left). Car spawns at the origin
    facing +X, centered between two parallel walls running the length of the
    corridor:

        +Y   ─────────────────────────────────────────────   <- left wall  (y=+CORRIDOR_HALF_WIDTH)
              car →
        -Y   ─────────────────────────────────────────────   <- right wall (y=-CORRIDOR_HALF_WIDTH)
             x=-2                                        x=14

    Corridor half-width 0.5 m (full width 1.0 m) is wide relative to the car's
    0.235 m track, so a working controller has real room to wander and correct
    rather than being pinned centered by geometry alone. Walls are thin boxes
    0.30 m tall, matching ramp_course.xml's wall convention.

    Ground plane: neoracer.xml's own floor geom lives on its worldbody as a
    sibling of the "car" body, so MjSpec.attach_body(car.body("car")) — the
    same composition pattern ramp_course.xml/manual_drive.py use — does NOT
    pull it into the composed scene (attach_body grafts only the named body's
    subtree). This track therefore carries its own floor below, matching
    neoracer.xml's plane geom (size/friction) so the composed scene has
    something for the car to rest on.
    -->

    <asset>
        <texture name="corridor_grid" type="2d" builtin="checker" width="512" height="512"
                 rgb1=".1 .2 .3" rgb2=".2 .3 .4"/>
        <material name="corridor_floor" texture="corridor_grid" texrepeat="1 1" texuniform="true"
                  reflectance=".2"/>
        <material name="wall" rgba=".55 .57 .60 1"/>
    </asset>

    <default>
        <default class="scenery">
            <geom type="box" material="wall" condim="3" friction="1.0 0.1 0.1"/>
        </default>
    </default>

    <worldbody>
        <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="9 1 .01" pos="6 0 0"
              material="corridor_floor" friction="1.5 0.1 0.1"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="corridor_wall_left"  pos="6 .5 .15" size="8 .02 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="corridor_wall_right" pos="6 -.5 .15" size="8 .02 .15"/>
    </worldbody>
</mujoco>
